   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 748 of the laws of 1991, amending the environmental\nconservation law and various other laws relating to establishing the Hudson\nriver valley greenway, in relation to extending the expiration of certain\nprovisions relating to indemnity to communities",
    "basePrintNo": "S9339",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9339-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §18, Chap 748 of 1991",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9339\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 748 of the laws of 1991, amending the environ-\nmental conservation law and various other laws relating to establishing\nthe Hudson river valley greenway, in relation to extending the expira-\ntion of certain provisions relating to indemnity to communities\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo provide a five year extension of the existing indemnity provision\nincluded in the Greenway Act of 1991 for communities in the Hudson River\nValley Greenway for certain actions related to their participation in\nthe Greenway Compact.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill would extend, until December 31, 2027, §\n44-0119(7) of the Environmental Conservation Law that provides indemnity\nfor communities in the Hudson River Valley Greenway for certain actions\nrelated to their participation in such compact.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the bill shall take effect imme-\ndiately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is necessary in order to help further the goals of the Green-\nway Act of 1991, and specifically, to help develop the Greenway Compact\nin the Hudson River Valley. Currently, communities that have adopted the\nGreenway Compact are indemnified by the state against lawsuits brought\nas a result of the purchase of land or land use controls or amendments\npursuant to the Compact. Those communities that have adopted the Compact\nwould lose this benefit if this subdivision were allowed to expire. Such\nan outcome could result in communities withdrawing their participation\nin the compact.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 190 of the Laws of 2017. Chapter 152 of the Laws of 2012.\n\nChapter 359 of the Laws of 2007. Chapter 138 of the Laws of 2002.\n\nChapter 342 of the Laws of 1997.\n\n \nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
